<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Alessandria</h1><p class="st-meta">1168 CE – 1348 CE (approx.) · capital Alessandria</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A new city founded by the Lombard League in 1168 and named after Pope Alexander III, which held out against Frederick Barbarossa's siege.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> founded Alessandria in 1168 at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanaro">Tanaro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bormida">Bormida</a>, settling people from nearby villages to block imperial allies such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-pavia">Pavia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/march-of-montferrat">March of Montferrat</a>. The city was named in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-iii">Pope Alexander III</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hastily fortified, Alessandria withstood a six-month siege by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> in 1174–1175, a key blow to the emperor before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Legnano</a>. In 1183 the city made peace with the emperor and was briefly renamed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-caesarea">Caesarea</a>. Governed by consuls and later a podestà, it fought its neighbours, especially the marquises of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, for control of the surrounding plain.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After periods under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> and other lords, Alessandria passed in 1348 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luchino-visconti-lord-of-milan">Luchino Visconti</a> and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. It passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-savoy">Duchy of Savoy</a> in 1707, a transfer confirmed in 1713.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1168 CE – 1348 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.95%;width:3.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1168 CE – 1348 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alessandria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Piedmontese, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alessandria</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1258&amp;focus=commune-of-alessandria" aria-label="Commune of Alessandria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4885 591 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Alessandria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5205 847L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5205 847h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5205 847h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Alessandria. <a href="/atlas?year=1258&amp;focus=commune-of-alessandria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

